<title>JAPAN: Fuji Oil closes 110,000 bpd topper for turnaround.</title>
<headline>Fuji Oil closes 110,000 bpd topper for turnaround.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fuji Oil Co Ltd said on Monday it had shut its 110,000 barrel-per-day (bpd) crude distillation unit (CDU) at its Sodegaura plant, near Tokyo, for regular maintenance checks.</p>
<p>The refiner plans to put the topper back on line on June 28, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>The other topper at the plant closed on May 13 for routine maintenance and is scheduled to resume operations on July 1.</p>
<p>Fuji Oil's turnaround schedule is as follows:</p>
<p>Facility		   Capacity			  Date</p>
<p>			 (barrels per day)</p>
<p>CDU			   52,000		    May 13 - July 1</p>
<p>CDU			  110,000		    May 19 - June 28</p>
<p>Vacuum distillation     55,000		    May 16 - June 30</p>
<p>Catalytic cracker	 15,500		    May 11 - July 6</p>
<p>Catalytic reformer	31,900		    May 13 - June 28</p>
<p>Naphtha desulphuriser   43,000		    May 13 - June 28</p>
<p>Kerosene/gas oil</p>
<p>    desulphuriser	 78,500		    May 15 - July 3</p>
<p>Indirect desulphuriser  47,000		    May 14 - July 3</p>
<p>Residual oil cracker    24,000		    May 15 - July 5</p>
<p>--Tokyo Energy Desk +81-3-3432-8837</p>
</text>
